# Band boundaries: Unicode CLDR 47 Day Period Rules, locale es
# (https://www.unicode.org/cldr/charts/47/supplemental/day_periods.html),
# transcribed in chronologia/dayparts.py as [06:00, 12:00).
# Sources: Diccionario de la lengua espanola, RAE (https://dle.rae.es/tarde).
# The bare word is NOT read here as the morning: "manana" is also the
# Spanish for tomorrow, and that reading wins unless an article, a
# demonstrative or "de" licenses the day-part one. See daypart_ref in
# lang.json, which omits the bare order for exactly this reason.
mañana
manana
